From: SF2000 Linux Port <sf2000-linux@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: accept bFLT HI16 pairs after their LO16 in text

MIPS compiler control flow can place a LUI in a branch delay slot after the
LO16 instruction which consumes the register at the backward branch target.
elf2flt preserves the semantic pair by ordering that HI16 relocation before
the LO16 relocation, even though the HI16 instruction has the higher text
address.

The SF2000 MIPS bFLT support incorrectly required every matching HI16 address
to be below its LO16 address.  sf2000-screen has three constructions of its
static HCGE context address: the ordinary LUI is relocated, but the two delay
slot LUIs are rejected and retain 0x0002.  Taking either branch therefore
passes 0x00027758 to memset instead of 0x84e27758.

Trust relocation-table order for the explicitly remembered latest HI16.  Also
update all prescanned HI16 instructions for the same original address,
including instructions above the LO16 in text.  Keep the backward instruction
scan as a conservative fallback when no explicit relocation state exists.

--- a/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h
+++ b/arch/mips/include/asm/flat.h
@@ -121,8 +121,7 @@ static inline int flat_mips_find_hi16_for_lo16(u32 __user *rp, u32 lo,
 		u32 candidate = ((flat_mips_hi16_insn & 0xffff) << 16) +
 				(s16)(lo & 0xffff);
 
-		if ((__force u32 *)flat_mips_hi16_rp < p &&
-		    flat_mips_addr_plausible(candidate)) {
+		if (flat_mips_addr_plausible(candidate)) {
 			*hi_rp = flat_mips_hi16_rp;
 			*hi_insn = flat_mips_hi16_insn;
 			return 1;
@@ -184,6 +183,5 @@ static inline int flat_mips_update_hi16_for_lo16(u32 __user *rp, u32 lo,
 						 u32 original, u32 addr)
 {
-	u32 *p = (__force u32 *)rp;
 	u32 rs = flat_mips_lo16_rs(lo);
 	int i, updated = 0;
 
@@ -193,7 +191,7 @@ static inline int flat_mips_update_hi16_for_lo16(u32 __user *rp, u32 lo,
 		u32 *scan = (__force u32 *)flat_mips_hi16_rps[i];
 		u32 candidate, hi;
 
-		if (!scan || scan >= p)
+		if (!scan)
 			continue;
 		hi = flat_mips_hi16_insns[i];
 		if (flat_mips_lui_rt(hi) != rs)
